---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';

// Everything claimed here is true of the code as built and was measured
// rather than assumed. Do not add a claim to this page that has not been
// tested — an accessibility statement that overstates is worse than none.
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How this website is built for accessibility, what has been tested, and what has not."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Accessibility"
    standfirst="What has been done, what has been measured, and what has not yet been tested."
  />

  <section class="field-light pad">
    <div class="wrap doc prose">
      <h2>The standard aimed at</h2>
      <p>
        WCAG 2.2 level AA is treated as the floor rather than the goal. Where the two conflict,
        being genuinely usable wins over being technically compliant.
      </p>

      <h2>What has been done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Every text and background pair on the site has been measured for contrast, including text
          sitting over the soft colour gradients behind the dark sections — which automated checkers
          cannot see. Thirty-seven pairs were tested and all meet or exceed the AA thresholds of
          4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for graphical marks. Several colours were changed during the
          build because measurement showed they fell short.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keyboard focus is always visible. The focus ring normally takes its colour from the text
          beside it, and the few filled controls where that would have been invisible against the
          page behind them carry their own ring colour instead. Every control was checked by
          comparing it focused and unfocused.
        </li>
        <li>
          The menu on small screens holds keyboard focus while it is open, closes on Escape, and
          returns you to the button you opened it with.
        </li>
        <li>A skip link to the main content is the first thing a keyboard reaches on every page.</li>
        <li>
          There are two slow, continuous movements: the tally marks on the home page drift gently,
          and the dark bands carry a very slow change of light. Both are deliberately below the
          threshold of noticing. If your system asks for reduced motion, every animation on the site
          stops completely — this was verified by measuring that not one pixel changes over three
          seconds.
        </li>
        <li>
          The tally figure on the home page carries a text description of what it shows, so it is
          not lost to a screen reader.
        </li>
        <li>
          Headings run in order without skipping levels, and the page is built from real landmarks —
          header, navigation, main, footer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Text reflows to a single column on small screens with no horizontal scrolling, which has
          been checked down to 320 pixels wide.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What has not been tested</h2>
      <p>
        The site has not been tested with a screen reader by someone who uses one daily, and it has
        not been through an independent audit. Measurement and automated checks are not a substitute
        for either.
      </p>

      <h2>If something does not work</h2>
      <p>
        If any part of this site is difficult or impossible for you to use, please say so — that is
        a fault worth fixing, and a description of what went wrong is genuinely useful.
        <a class="link" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 90;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .doc h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .doc ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }
  .doc li {
    padding-left: var(--s-5);
    position: relative;
  }
  .doc li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 10px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--marigold-dark);
  }
</style>
